{{Documentation subpage}}
Utilising the alpha3 ISO 4217 code. For example, the code number can be derived from the code. Based on the ISO 4217 Standfard definition (per {{tl|ISO 4217/cite}}, {{as of|lc=yes|October 2022}}).

There are '''304 unique codes''' ({{mono|1=ADP..ZWR}}). Codes are reused (as currency in history, in history with different end-date by country, in List Two funds, in entities) resulting in '''452 currency definitions''' (data rows).

* {{Property|P498}}

==General==
: {{para|iso-code}}
: {{para|format}}
: {{para|is-obsolete}}

Most parameters work by {{tl|yesno}} principle: {{code|1=yes, 1, true, <anytext>}} and {{code|1=no, 0, false, <blank>}} are recognised as T/F.
:See also {{slink||maintenance-category ISO 4217}}

:{{para|format}}-options can be comma-separated list: {{para|format|option-none, ISO4217-cat, mono, brackets, }} (as announced per template)

==Base: iso-code==
===ISO 4217/code===
* {{tl|ISO 4217/code}}
Returns valid ISO 4217 code ''or'' blank.
: {{para|iso-code}}

:Basic: {{para|format|&lt;blank&gt;}} returns EITHER the code as exists OR &lt;blank&gt; (no tracking etc)

: {{para|format|option-none, ISO4217-cat}}

:See {{slink||maintenance-category ISO4217}}

Other data (ref, comment) elsewhere. 
Data {{As of |lc=yes|17 October 2022}}, per source {{tl|ISO 4217/cite}}

