==Derived value templates==
===minor unit===
* "Minor unit" in ISO 4217: number of decimals for ''minor unit'' used in currency trade. For example, {{mono|USD}} has {{mono|1=Minor unit=2}}, i.e. {{val|0.01}} (dollarcent unit). 
Occurring values are: {{code|1=<blank>, N.A., 0, 2, 3, 4}}. So, incidentally, {{code|1}} (for {{val|p={{cursign}}&nbsp;0.1}}) is not present.
Obsolete currency (historical, List Three): has no minor unit ("blank").

* {{tl|ISO 4217/code-minor-unit}}
:In enwiki: "&lt;blank>", "N.A.", "0" all return blank, because "{{val|1|p={{cursign}}&nbsp;}}" is not a subunit of "{{val|1|p={{cursign}}&nbsp;}}".

: {{para|iso-code}}, {{para|is-obsolete}}, {{para|format|blank/default (0.001-form), exponent (N.A., &lt;blank&gt;, 0, 2, 3, 4)}}
;Examples
:'''&lt;blank>''' {{mono|1=AFA}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=AFA|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=AFA}}
:'''N.A.''' {{mono|1=XPD}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=XPD|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=XPD}}
:'''0''' {{mono|1=KRW}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=KRW}}
:'''1''' (not present)
:'''2''' {{mono|1=RUB}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=RUB|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=RUB}}
:'''3''' {{mono|1=OMR}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=OMR|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=OMR}}
:'''4''' {{mono|1=CLF}}: {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=CLF|format=exponent}} &rarr; {{ISO 4217/code-minor-unit|iso-code=CLF}}

====Ambiguous code and minor units====
* 10 codes are ''ambiguous'': they appear both ''obsolete'' and ''active'': {{code|1=<nowiki>|ANG|EUR|HRK|IDR|MWK|PEN|RON|SDG|SZL|TRY</nowiki>}}.
:For example, {{mono|PEN}} refers to an obsolete ''and'' an active currency. These have different exponents.
:{{para|is-obsolete|no/yes}} sets the right one. Default is: {{para|is-obsolete|no}} (currency {{mono|PEN}} is active}})
