===code-is-ambiguous===
* 10 codes are ambiguous, they appear both ''obsolete'' and ''active'': {{code|1=<nowiki>|ANG|EUR|HRK|IDR|MWK|PEN|RON|SDG|SZL|TRY</nowiki>}}.
:For example, {{mono|EUR}} is active in {{smallcaps2|1=GERMANY}}, and obsolete in {{smallcaps2|1=SERBIA AND MONTENEGRO}} per {{mono|1=withdrawal-date=2006-10}} (List Three). {{As of|17 October 2022}}.

:When such code is used, disambiguation may be required ({{mono|1=is-obsolete=yes/no}}), to specify which currency is intended. This is relevant with minor-unit, and manually setting (clarifying){{mono|1=is-obsolete}}. Used in {{tlf|Infobox currency}}.

